Here's a simple SystemVerilog module for an LDPC (Low-Density Parity-Check) encoder. This implementation assumes a parallel input data stream and generates the corresponding encoded output stream.

```verilog
module ldpc_encoder(
    input wire clk,
    input wire reset,
    input wire data[],
    output wire encoded[]
);

reg [7:0] state;
reg [7:0] input;
reg [7:0] output;

initial begin
    state <= 8'b00000000;
    input <= 8'b00000000;
end

always @(posedge clk or posedge reset) begin
    if (reset)
        state <= 8'b00000000;
    else
        state <= state + 1;

    input <= data[];
    output <= encode(state, input);
end

function [7:0] encode(state, input);
    // Implementation of LDPC encoding algorithm goes here
    // ...
endfunction

assign encoded[i] = output[i];

endmodule
```

This module has an `ldpc_encoder` top-level instance with inputs `clk`, `reset`, `data[]`, and outputs `encoded[]`. The module also contains an `encode` function that implements the LDPC encoding algorithm. You can replace the `// ...` comment with your preferred LDPC encoding logic.

