          "type": "Single",
          "availability": [
            {
              "startDate": ISODate("2022-01-01T00:00:00Z"),
              "endDate": ISODate("2022-03-31T00:00:00Z"),
              "status": "Available"
            },
            // ... other availability periods ...
          ]
        },
        // ... other rooms ...
      ]
    },
    // ... other hotels ...
  ]
}
```

This schema uses a collection called `hotels` to store information about each hotel property. Each hotel has a unique `_id` and a `name`. The `rooms` array contains information about all the rooms in the hotel, including their number, type, and availability.

The `availability` array contains information about when each room is available for reservation. Each availability period is represented as a document with a `startDate`, `endDate`, and `status` field. The `status` field can be set to `Available`, `Booked`, or `Unavailable` to indicate whether the room is currently available for reservation.

By storing this data in a NoSQL database like MongoDB, you can quickly and easily retrieve information about hotel rooms and their availability, even when dealing with large datasets.

